the-firm-as-one-program-39 = unlines (cons "- **C16** Knowledge belongs to the firm, not to individuals, and onboarding is a walk ([P2: Programs, relations and their justifications in one language, with the reasoning kept as data (hyperactivity v31 §1–2)], [P9: Content-addressed, decentralized exchange of code with its proofs (hyperactivity v31 §10.8)])." (cons "  What a person understood becomes a definition with its rationale, still valid when they go home and still valid when they leave. Key-person risk, and much of what garden leave and non-competes pay for, comes from the firm being unable to separate knowledge from the person. A new hire walks the firm's information space in order, as an agent walks this repository, and becomes productive in days instead of most of a year." nil))
